# Test hard rules

Every `[Fact]` / `[Theory]` method **must** contain these three comments, in order:

```
// Arrange
// Act
// Assert
```

Do not skip a section. Setup (fixtures, `GetMock`, `Build`/`Create`, SUT) goes under Arrange. The single operation under test goes under Act. Assertions go under Assert.

## Fictional names only

Test source must not contain real team names, league names, competitions, or streaming sites. Use labels like `Home United`, `Away City`, `League Alpha`, `Channel North`, `https://streams.example.com/...`. Identify captured HTML fixtures by scores, status, or minute — not by club or competition names.

## Specimens

- Create data with **AutoFixture** (`IFixture` from `AutoMoqFixture.Create()`).
- Use `_fixture.Build<T>().With(...).Create()` or `_fixture.Create<T>()` in the test — do not hand-build object graphs with `new Stream { ... }` / `new Game { ... }`.
- Collaborator mocks: `_fixture.GetMock<IFoo>()` — **never** `new Mock<IFoo>()`.
- `GetMock` freezes the mock so `_fixture.Create<Sut>()` receives the same instance.

```csharp
[Fact]
public async Task Resolve_WhenHealthy_ReturnsUrl()
{
    // Arrange
    var stream = _fixture.Build<Stream>().With(s => s.Url, url).Create();
    var lan = _fixture.GetMock<ILocalLanPlayService>();
    lan.Setup(...).ReturnsAsync(m3u8);
    var sut = _fixture.Create<StreamResolver>();

    // Act
    var result = await sut.ResolveM3U8UrlAsync(stream, referer);

    // Assert
    Assert.Equal(m3u8.Url, result);
}
```
